{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:11:57.290026647Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"dd202751-dc0c-4381-9875-7f70cff422fc","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=builder existence CONFIRMED — no divergence next=join G1 claim against artifact evidence blocker=none\n\nCONFIRMATION (trigger 1 staleness: NOT fired; trigger 2 mismatch: NOT fired). Evidence the builder is alive and on-plan:\n- Lock: #277 claimed 2026-08-08 06:05 (crosslink locks list).\n- Position: --kind plan comment id=1064 at 06:09:31 enumerating G1-G10 + claim-verification pass, consistent with the #277 plan + addendum (authoritative scope).\n- Heartbeat: --kind observation id=1065 at 06:09:42 — 'state=working ... next=G1: write+run tests/measure_poc_size.py, rewrite report.md 5.3'.\n- Cadence: builder started 06:05, first position 06:09:31 (~4.5m). Against a 15-20m milestone interval the 2x staleness threshold is ~06:40. Not stale.\n\nI explicitly RETRACT the absence signal I flagged in my prior checkpoint (no pp3g-hE4M worktree/branch). It was correctly withheld rather than called. Resolution: the builder reuses the existing C2 worktree per the plan's OWNERSHIP clause, so no hE4M worktree was ever going to exist.\n\n[CONCERN — process/provenance, NOT work divergence] Builder identity mismatch between dispatch and store. The #278 description and my dispatch brief name the builder 'pp3g-hE4M', but the durable store attributes all of it to 'pp3g-qfOy-investigation-task-decision-ready-comparison-not-a' (holder of the #277 lock at 06:05 and of #264 since 04:39). 'pp3g-hE4M' appears in NO channel: no worktree, no feature/ branch, no crosslink/agents/ branch, no comment author. Impact: (a) the in-flight monitor is told to track an identifier that by construction can never appear, which is precisely the PVi7 false-positive condition on #228 — same shared-worktree/shared-identity root cause, one layer up in the naming; (b) provenance for this execution is co-mingled with the prior investigation agent that produced the very artifact under audit (7dd054be + af350f49), so 'who produced the revision' is not separable in the store from 'who produced the thing being revised'. Recommended mitigation (orchestrator, not me): record the dispatch-name-to-store-identity mapping on #277 at dispatch time whenever a builder reuses an existing worktree.\n\n[CONCERN — tooling, affects future auditors] 'crosslink kickoff list' documents itself as listing agents across worktrees, tmux and Docker, but returned 'No kickoff agents found' while 29 worktrees demonstrably exist (git worktree list). A channel that reports zero for known-present entities is uninformative and must NOT be used as absence evidence by a divergence verifier. Flagging so it is not mistaken for a signal.","created_at":"2026-08-08T06:11:57.282984786Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA2GmrZV/y6PqFyJ1WcWBuOPdypf/7vMHD8k6fnvy49ooCgYeuoiOFV5xILLyFLjvdkOHUw0TJRBpPabPEYNOeAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKj6VMaNbs/tBh4AE1cHLF1CsmReVsNrN4JLyeAAJYlyh0COwLCK36xMje2EnY5mXjUARgr+3oqivlAA7Ec+Vw8="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:13:49.725733483Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"75d4326f-9b31-4182-85d8-19ba495743f8","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[VERIFY] state=verifying completed=G1 claim-vs-artifact join — CONFIRMED on substance, one forward-looking presentational risk flagged next=continue polling G2-G10 blocker=none\n\n== G1 JOIN: claim CONFIRMED ==\nBuilder claim (position id=1065, 06:09:42): 'next=G1: write+run tests/measure_poc_size.py, rewrite report.md 5.3'.\nArtifact evidence found (git -C on the execution worktree pp3g-qfOy, working tree):\n- ?? research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/tests/measure_poc_size.py — EXISTS (was ABSENT at baseline af350f49)\n- ?? research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/c2-gap-investigation/logs/measure-poc-size.log — EXISTS (was ABSENT at baseline)\nBoth are new, both are inside the repo (not /tmp), so the #271/playbook-5.9 artifact rule is satisfied so far. Not yet committed — expected at this stage.\n\nContent join against the plan's required G1 figures: log emits total=147, strict_code=64, mechanism_proper=57 — an EXACT match to the numbers both Phase-2 audits independently re-derived. The script derives these via tokenize (independent derivation), then hard-asserts them and exits 1 on mismatch — this implements hy3 S1's exact mitigation (committed counter script, no agent-computed metric) rather than restating it.\n\n== [CONCERN — LOW/MED, presentational, flagged NOW because 5.3 is not yet written] ==\nlogs/measure-poc-size.log lists FIVE flat component lines:\n  _is_schema_validation_error=5, SchemaAwareConnectionManager_class_body=20, _call_persistent_override=16, _register_async=22, register_with_connection=10\nA reader summing those five gets 73, while the next line asserts sum_components=57. Nothing in the log marks WHY.\n\nI verified the arithmetic is CORRECT, not wrong: in measure_poc_size.py, class_body=code_range(65,103) and override=code_range(79,103), and intercept_poc.py (af350f49) confirms _call_persistent is a METHOD INSIDE SchemaAwareConnectionManager. The override's 16 lines are therefore already counted within class_body's 20, and sum_components deliberately excludes it (5+20+22+10=57) to avoid double-counting. The script is right.\n\nThe risk is that the LOG DOES NOT SAY SO. If report.md 5.3's rewritten table reproduces this flat five-row list, the published table will not visibly reconcile to its own headline — which is precisely the defect G1 exists to eliminate (the original 5+20+22+10=57 vs headline 48 non-reconciliation, hy3 C3 / big-pickle R1). Re-deriving auditors would land on 73 vs 57 and re-open the finding.\nCheap fix available to the builder while 5.3 is still unwritten: mark the override row as nested (e.g. 'of which _call_persistent override: 16') or emit an explicit 'excluded_from_sum=_call_persistent_override(nested)' field. Flag only — I do not fix.\n\n== [OBSERVATION — minor, durability] ==\nmeasure_poc_size.py pins component boundaries as hardcoded physical line ranges (44-51, 55, 58-62, 65-103, 79-103, 106-133, 136-147) AND hardcodes the expected totals in its pass gate. Correct and self-checking for the current intercept_poc.py revision, but it silently mis-slices if that file ever changes. Appropriate for a one-shot reconciliation artifact; worth one sentence in 5.3 stating the script is revision-pinned to intercept_poc.py at af350f49.\n\nTriggers 1 (staleness) and 3/4: NOT fired. Builder on-plan and on-cadence.","created_at":"2026-08-08T06:13:49.720035141Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAi49CJDcPjQL4+S/M+j