{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:16:36.353980794Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"1c5e4890-6ffd-494d-a154-27d187494c08","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[VERIFY] state=verifying completed=G2 (the HIGH gap) independently CONFIRMED closed by directly-measured evidence; G6 partly closed; G4 n>=3 runs in progress next=poll G3/G5/G7-G10 + final commit blocker=none\n\n== G2 JOIN: CONFIRMED — claim now TESTED, not inferred ==\nArtifacts (new since baseline af350f49, timestamped 06:14:17-06:14:23, i.e. produced in-flight during this dispatch):\n- tests/phase_b2b_preabsorbed.py\n- logs/phase-b2b-preabsorbed-harness.log\n- logs/phase-b2b-preabsorbed-proxy.log\nDecisive line: 'B2B_RESULT pass=True preabsorb_interception_fired=True add1_error_preserved=True warm_add_error_preserved=True other_tool_success=True spawns=1 proxies=2 reconnect=False schema_validation_failures=2'.\n\nEvery element of the plan's G2 Verify line reproduces:\n- 1 spawn — backend_spawn_count=1 (single instance be-1-1390891-60304).\n- 1 persistent proxy — persistent_proxies=1.\n- no reconnect — reconnect_fired=False.\n- verbatim ErrorResult — INVOKE add(2,3) ok=False outcome_type=ErrorResult with the full message_verbatim preserved.\n- interception actually in the path — the traceback runs through intercept_poc.py:90 in _call_persistent, then client.py:133, session.py:1064, session.py:1110. This is mechanism proof, not just an outcome match: the SDK origin at session.py:1110 and the override seam both appear in one stack.\n- pre-absorbed genuinely established — call order multiply-first-then-add, with 'B2B_BEGIN pre-absorb call multiply' succeeding (20.0) BEFORE the drift call, so the stale schema is absorbed first. Correct A2b pattern.\n\n== [OK] proxies=2 is NOT a Verify-line miss — convention matches baseline ==\nI checked this specifically because the plan says '1 proxy' while the log says proxies=2. The harness reports two distinct fields, and B2b's pair is IDENTICAL to the pre-existing B2 baseline: B2_SPAWN_COUNTS backend_spawn_count=1 proxy_processes=2 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False. proxy_processes counts the short-lived registration/discovery connection plus the persistent one; persistent_proxies is the criterion figure. No divergence. Recommendation (presentational, same class as my G1 note): when 7 states B2b at '1 proxy', cite persistent_proxies=1 and note proxy_processes=2, so a re-deriving auditor does not read 2 as a criterion failure.\n\n== Cross-phase result: the 8 claim is now directly measured ==\nPlacing B2b against the committed baselines:\n- A1 control: spawns=2, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect=True\n- A2b Option A pre-absorbed: spawns=2, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect=True, heal_events=1 (Option A DEGRADES pre-absorbed)\n- B2 Option B fresh: spawns=1, persistent_proxies=1, reconnect=False\n- B2b Option B pre-absorbed (NEW): spawns=1, persistent_proxies=1, reconnect=False — identical to fresh\nSo Option B's invariance across fresh and pre-absorbed is now a measured result. Under the addendum's 'tested = directly measured only' convention, 8 may legitimately keep the word tested for this claim. hy3 C1 / big-pickle R3 — the top HIGH condition — is substantively closed. This is the single most important thing this dispatch had to do, and the evidence is real.\n\n== G6 partly closed by the same run ==\nB2b also recorded the two B-side gaps: warm repeat add(1,1) delta_ms=9 ok=False with error preserved (warm-call), and other-tool multiply(6,7) ok=True after the failure (other-tool-untouched). Both were G6 requirements; the builder got them from one phase rather than a separate run — efficient and legitimate, though 6/7 should cite phase-b2b for them.\n\n== G4 in progress ==\nlogs/n3/ now holds phase-a1-control run1/run2/run3 (06:15:16/27/37) and phase-a2-selfheal-c2-run1 (06:15:49). All three A1 runs agree exactly (spawns=2, proxy_processes=3, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect=True) — good reproducibility for the n>=3 requirement. B2 n>=3 not yet observed.\n\n== Position vs artifact: a note for the topology record ==\nNo divergence, but the direction of lag is worth recording: the builder's last durable position is still id=1065 (06:09:42, 'next=G1'), while artifacts prove G1 done, G2 done, G6 partly done and G4 underway as of 06:15:49. Artifact evidence LED position evidence by roughly 6-10 minutes here. Staleness alone would therefore have understated progress; the artifact join is what carried the signal. Not yet stale (2x threshold ~06:40) and liveness is independently proven by file timestamps.","created_at":"2026-08-08T06:16:36.346850866Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAduhZy7zl7EJMKv7duHI6yIkOE78HG/zdubRyrxGyi7zSi6gA8bd5BgAPvktvRpc4nQz8NvDP1TV4VobQ32JDCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH9GIZQjyOrzME/u7wkHzRdxQ9nxQ3WmGt7IYvL9zj+3u8nRrGGhadKnpGQEY0LdOM1gZmUFKEi/yp8ZKMsgOgs="}
